  "description": "The Macho King LTD is a special small batch run of completes in a real nice color with a real nice parts spec, SRAM Force 22 Hydraulic. We are only building 50 of them and expect them to go fast. If you would like one, get to your local shop and make sure they reserve one for you.\n\nThe Macho King is a special one.\n\nThroughout your bike life, some will come and some will go, and some will touch your heart and make you wish to hold onto them forever. The Macho King is one of those. It is simply the very best cross bike we have ever made available, and if you are lucky enough to lay hands on one, you're going to love it.\n\nFirst off it's made from Reynolds 853 tubing which is, in our estimation, the finest steel going. You know what's awesome about buying a steel bike with really nice tubes? Everything. It's super high quality and will always be super high quality. Nothing holds it's value like high end steel, it's lightweight and smooths out the bumps like only it can.\n\nPerhaps you love steel frames but prefer a carbon fork. No problem, this baby comes with a tapered carbon steerer Whisky No. 7 fork and a 44mm headtube to accomodate it. The fork saves about a lb and a quarter over our steel variant.\n\nYou ride your bike all the time on road and off, through all conditions? How about some disc brakes for maximum control.\n\nYou see what we're saying? This is the one.\n\nIt retains all the All-City custom touches such as: signature dropouts, signature seat collar, custom English threaded bottom bracket shell, internal cable routing for the front derailleur, reinforcements on the bottle bosses, and fender mounts.\n\nIt has clearance for 38's plus room for tons of mud, our proven cyclocross geometry, and the All-City name backing it all up.\n\nThis thing is amazing, ride one and see for yourself.\n\nReynolds 853 tubeset: The finest steel, saves weight and soaks up bumps\n\nED Finish: The entire bike is E.D. coated inside and out. E.D. coating not only improves the quality and durability of the paint, but is the best rust preventative we know of. (same as Macho Disc)\n\nSignature Disc Dropouts: Custom AC two piece disc dropouts complete the package. It's the little touches that help our bikes stand apart. (same as Macho Man Disc)\n\n44mm headtube & tapered steerer fork: Maximum stiffness and control in the front end\n\nFender Compatible: We hope you ride this bike in all conditions all year long, so with that in mind we added fender mounts. (same as Macho Man Disc)",
